{"id": "bart-contract-conflicts-disgorgement", "title": "BART voided contracts after conflict findings and declined to pursue $1,249,066", "seconds": 55.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "made": "2026-11-26", "key": "1c8a335305c526ec", "words": 168, "beats": [{"scene": "contracts", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "BART’s Inspector General examined three allegations about employee contracting decisions.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.34, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["What", "happened", "to", "the", "contract", "payments?"], "sub": "BART Inspector General"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.76, 1.09, 1.48, 1.76, 2.36, 2.58, 2.97, 3.53]}, {"scene": "contracts", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The Inspector General found that two employees violated California’s contract conflict-of-interest law.", "t0": 4.46, "t1": 9.86, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "report", "kicker": "BART Office of the Inspector General", "text": "Section 1090", "mark": "Section 1090"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.59, 0.97, 1.23, 1.38, 1.67, 2.41, 2.95, 3.61, 4.18, 5.08]}, {"scene": "contracts", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]", "suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "One former employee set up a firm. BART paid it more than a million dollars.", "t0": 9.98, "t1": 13.91, "shot": "r2", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Payments after the decisions", "heading": "Two former employees’ firms", "source": "report", "rows": [{"icon": "contract", "label": "Former evaluator’s firm", "value": "$1,041,309"}, {"icon": "contract", "label": "New employer", "value": "$207,757"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.56, 0.99, 1.15, 1.26, 1.33, 2.12, 2.47, 2.71, 2.8, 2.95, 3.09, 3.16, 3.45]}, {"scene": "contracts", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "A second employee helped make four contracts after accepting a position with the firm.", "t0": 14.03, "t1": 17.72, "shot": "r3", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "report", "kicker": "BART Office of the Inspector General", "text": "Four contracts", "mark": "Four contracts"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.43, 0.85, 1.11, 1.29, 1.51, 2.0, 2.23, 2.61, 2.67, 3.04, 3.17, 3.28]}, {"scene": "contracts", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "BART paid 207,757 dollars to the other employee’s new employer.", "t0": 17.84, "t1": 23.02, "shot": "r4", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "New employer"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.48, 0.7, 0.97, 1.26, 1.77, 2.06, 2.32, 2.88, 3.64, 3.8, 3.93, 4.14, 4.55, 4.68]}, {"scene": "contracts", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "The Inspector General recommended pursuing the return of 1,249,066 dollars.", "t0": 23.14, "t1": 27.55, "shot": "r5", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$1,249,066", "label": "Disgorgement recommended by the Inspector General"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.6, 0.92, 1.48, 1.93, 2.05, 2.42, 2.54, 2.79, 2.99, 3.28, 3.56, 3.87]}, {"scene": "response", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "BART voided the agreements. It declined the recommendation to pursue the payments.", "t0": 27.77, "t1": 31.55, "shot": "r6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "annual23", "kicker": "BART Office of the Inspector General", "text": "FY2023 annual report", "mark": "FY2023 annual report"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.63, 0.73, 1.44, 1.6, 2.01, 2.11, 2.75, 2.85, 3.14, 3.23]}, {"scene": "response", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["defense[0]"], "text": "BART said the contractors delivered valuable services.", "t0": 31.67, "t1": 34.18, "shot": "r7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Agency response"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.46, 0.57, 1.15, 1.5, 1.9]}, {"scene": "response", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "In a third procurement, the district disqualified a bidder before award.", "t0": 34.3, "t1": 37.49, "shot": "r8", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "report", "kicker": "BART Office of the Inspector General", "text": "Third procurement", "mark": "Third procurement"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.24, 0.48, 1.03, 1.15, 1.5, 2.12, 2.17, 2.45, 2.77]}, {"scene": "response", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "That decision prevented a potential violation.", "t0": 37.61, "t1": 39.56, "shot": "r9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "No payment"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.56, 0.94, 0.99, 1.35]}, {"scene": "response", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "In 2024 the Board barred former officials from contractor work for 12 months after departure.", "t0": 39.68, "t1": 44.32, "shot": "r10", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "code", "kicker": "San Francisco Bay Area Rapid Transit District Board of Directors", "text": "December 2024 Contractor Code", "mark": "December 2024 Contractor Code"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.35, 1.04, 1.18, 1.41, 1.68, 1.97, 2.42, 2.6, 3.13, 3.34, 3.46, 3.7, 3.91, 4.13]}, {"scene": "response", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "The proposed employee code revision was still under review in fiscal 2026.", "t0": 44.44, "t1": 48.43, "shot": "r11", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "annual26", "kicker": "BART Office of the Inspector General", "text": "FY2026 annual report", "mark": "FY2026 annual report"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.49, 0.88, 1.15, 1.55, 1.67, 1.93, 2.15, 2.49, 2.6, 3.01, 3.28]}, {"scene": "response", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "The recommended amount does not establish that BART lost or recovered that sum.", "t0": 48.55, "t1": 52.15, "shot": "r12", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Recovery", "Financial loss"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.66, 0.97, 1.16, 1.33, 1.78, 1.93, 2.24, 2.6, 2.73, 3.11, 3.26]}, {"scene": "response", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 52.27, "t1": 54.41, "shot": "r13", "visual": {"type": "en